---
import HobbyVideo from '~/components/HobbyVideo.astro'
import LayoutDefault from '~/layouts/LayoutDefault.astro'
---

<LayoutDefault
  title="Music & my hi-fi system — Gordan Grgić"
  image="/og/hifi.jpg"
  imageAlt="My hi-fi system with Polk R700 speakers, amplifier and touch-screen streamer"
  description="My personal hi-fi system, with self-assembled speaker cables, a Linux Mint streamer and a love of everyday listening."
>
  <article class="hifi-page">
    <a href="/hobbies/">← All hobbies</a>
    <header>
      <p class="folio-label">MUSIC / HANDS-ON AUDIO</p><h1>Music & my hi-fi system</h1><p>
        Music is part of my everyday life. I put this system together around the way I listen, and made the cables
        myself. The small details of connecting everything are part of the enjoyment.
      </p>
    </header>
    <figure class="system-photo">
      <img
        src="/images/hobbies/hifi/system.webp"
        alt="My hi-fi system with Polk R700 speakers, amplifier and touch-screen streamer"
        width="1448"
        height="1086"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </figure>
    <section>
      <h2 id="cables">Cables I made myself</h2><p>
        I assembled the cables for my own system using Van den Hul CS – 122 HYBRID speaker cable and Van den Hul
        connectors. Choosing the lengths and fitting the connectors let me adapt the wiring to the equipment and its
        position in the room.
      </p>
      <div class="cable-photos">
        <figure>
          <img
            src="/images/hobbies/hifi/speaker-cables-jumpers-v2.webp"
            alt="Close-up of the speaker cables and connectors I assembled"
            width="1086"
            height="1448"
            loading="lazy"
            data-group="hifi"
            data-index="2"
          /><figcaption>My speaker cable and replacement jumpers at the speaker terminals.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <a href="https://www.vandenhul.com/product/cs-122-hybrid-halogen-free/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Cable specifications ↗</a
      >
      <h3>Speaker jumpers I made myself</h3>
      <p>
        I was not happy with the factory terminal links on my Polk R700 speakers, so I made replacement jumpers using
        Oehlbach Silverline SP-40 cable (silver-plated copper, 2 × 4 mm²) and Viborg VB401R banana plugs.
      </p>
      <p>After the change, the bass sounded much more powerful to me.</p>
      <p>
        <a
          href="https://oehlbach.com/en/cableconfigurator/loudspeaker/one-amplifier/single-connection-on-the-speaker/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Oehlbach cable configurator ↗</a
        >
        ·
        <a
          href="https://www.audiophonics.fr/en/banana-plugs/viborg-vb401r-p-18654.html"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Banana plug details ↗</a
        >
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 id="power-cable">A power cable I assembled</h2>
      <p>
        I also assembled the power cable for my hi-fi system. This photograph shows the mains plug and braided cable.
      </p>
      <figure class="power-cable-photo">
        <img
          src="/images/hobbies/hifi/handmade-power-cable-v2.webp"
          width="1086"
          height="1448"
          loading="lazy"
          alt="The mains plug and braided power cable I assembled for my hi-fi system"
          data-group="hifi-power-cable"
          data-index="0"
        />
        <figcaption>My assembled power cable</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>The system I listen to</h2><div class="equipment-grid">
        <article class="equipment-card speaker-equipment">
          <img src="/images/hobbies/hifi/speaker.webp" alt="Polk R700" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy" /><div
            class="equipment-copy"
          >
            <p class="equipment-role">Speakers</p><h3>Polk R700</h3><p>
              The R700 uses a ring-radiator tweeter, a 6.5-inch midrange driver and two 8-inch woofers. Separate drivers
              cover different frequency ranges, while its Power Port 2.0 bass-reflex system extends the low-frequency
              output. Speaker position and the room still influence the result.
            </p><p class="equipment-note">The granite slab provides a rigid, level base beneath the speaker feet.</p><a
              href="https://www.polkaudio.com/en-us/product/home-speakers/floor-standing/reserve-r700/300035.html"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Manufacturer ↗</a
            >
          </div>
        </article><article class="equipment-card">
          <img
            src="/images/hobbies/hifi/amplifier.jpg"
            alt="Yamaha A-S1200"
            width="800"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
          /><p class="equipment-role">Amplifier</p><h3>Yamaha A-S1200</h3><p>
            The A-S1200 combines volume control and power amplification in one unit. A toroidal transformer supplies the
            amplifier, and its floating balanced power stage drives the speakers. In this setup, the external DAC
            handles digital conversion before the signal reaches the Yamaha.
          </p><a
            href="https://europe.yamaha.com/en/products/audio_visual/hifi_components/a-s1200/index.html"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Manufacturer ↗</a
          >
        </article><article class="equipment-card">
          <img src="/images/hobbies/hifi/dac.jpg" alt="Topping E70 Velvet" width="800" height="500" loading="lazy" /><p
            class="equipment-role"
          >
            DAC
          </p><h3>Topping E70 Velvet</h3><p>
            The E70 Velvet uses an AK4499EX DAC chip to convert digital audio into an analogue line-level signal for the
            amplifier. Keeping conversion in a dedicated device gives the Linux streamer a separate audio output stage.
            The source format, playback software and output settings determine the digital signal delivered to the DAC.
          </p><a href="https://www.toppingaudio.com/product-item/e70-velvet" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Manufacturer ↗</a
          >
        </article><article class="equipment-card">
          <img
            src="/images/hobbies/hifi/display-linux-mint-v2.webp"
            alt="My 14-inch touch display running Linux Mint with a compact keyboard"
            width="1448"
            height="1086"
            loading="lazy"
            data-group="hifi-display"
            data-index="0"
          /><p class="equipment-note">My 14-inch touch display</p>
          <p class="equipment-role">Streamer</p><h3>MeLE Quieter4C Mini PC</h3><p>
            The Quieter4C is a fanless mini PC, so cooling adds no fan noise to the listening space. Linux Mint runs the
            playback software, while the 14-inch touch display provides local control. Bit-perfect playback depends on
            the software and audio configuration passing the original samples through without resampling or digital
            volume changes.
          </p><p>14-inch touch display · Linux Mint</p><p>
            I use the MeLE Quieter4C Mini PC with Linux Mint as a streamer, configured for bit-perfect playback in my
            listening setup.
          </p><a href="https://forum.mele.cn/product/Quieter4C-en.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Manufacturer ↗</a
          >
        </article><article class="equipment-card">
          <p class="equipment-role">Speaker cable &amp; connectors</p><h3>
            Van den Hul CS – 122 HYBRID (halogen free)
          </h3><p>
            The CS – 122 HYBRID has a conductor cross-section of 2.96 mm² per lead and a halogen-free jacket. Conductor
            size and cable length affect resistance between amplifier and speaker. I assembled the leads with Van den
            Hul connectors; secure termination and consistent polarity are the practical details at each end.
          </p><p>Van den Hul connectors · assembled by me</p><a
            href="https://www.vandenhul.com/product/cs-122-hybrid-halogen-free/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Manufacturer ↗</a
          >
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="room-measurements">Room measurements &amp; speaker placement</h2>
      <p>I used my miniDSP UMIK-1 microphone with Room EQ Wizard (REW) to measure my listening room.</p>
      <p>
        The measurements showed more pronounced bass from the left speaker, which was closer to a wall. I used these
        measurements to guide speaker placement and find the sweet spot in my room.
      </p>
      <div class="room-measurement-images">
        <figure class="measurement-microphone">
          <img
            src="/images/hobbies/hifi/umik-1.webp"
            width="304"
            height="350"
            loading="lazy"
            alt="miniDSP UMIK-1 USB measurement microphone with its stand"
            data-group="room-measurements"
            data-index="0"
          />
          <figcaption>UMIK-1 measurement microphone · Product photograph by miniDSP</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img
            src="/images/hobbies/hifi/rew-measurement-example.webp"
            width="640"
            height="416"
            loading="lazy"
            alt="Illustrative REW frequency-response measurement from the miniDSP guide"
            data-group="room-measurements"
            data-index="1"
          />
          <figcaption>
            Illustrative REW measurement from the miniDSP guide.
            <a
              href="https://www.minidsp.com/applications/acoustic-measurements/acoustic-measurements"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Example source ↗</a
            >
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p>
        <a href="https://www.minidsp.com/products/acoustic-measurement/umik-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >UMIK-1 microphone ↗</a
        >
        ·
        <a href="https://www.roomeqwizard.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Room EQ Wizard (REW) ↗</a>
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 id="listening-testing">Listening room — testing<span class="testing-dots" aria-hidden="true">...</span></h2>
      <h3>The system in use</h3><p>A short recording of my listening setup.</p><HobbyVideo
        portrait={false}
        src="/videos/hifi/system-test.mp4"
        poster="/images/hobbies/hifi/video-poster.jpg"
        label="The system in use"
      />
      <p>Two longer recordings from listening sessions at home.</p><div class="listening-videos">
        <figure>
          <HobbyVideo
            src="/videos/hifi/listening-1.mp4"
            poster="/images/hobbies/hifi/listening-1-poster.jpg"
            label="Listening session 1"
          /><figcaption>Listening session 1</figcaption>
        </figure><figure>
          <HobbyVideo
            src="/videos/hifi/listening-2.mp4"
            poster="/images/hobbies/hifi/listening-2-poster.jpg"
            label="Listening session 2"
          /><figcaption>Listening session 2</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>From listening to MILA</h2>
      <p>Press play and listen to your heart’s content.</p><p>
        Living with a music system also made me think about the interface I wanted to use every day. That interest led
        to MILA, my personal audio streamer project.
      </p><a href="/projects/mila/">Explore the MILA project →</a>
    </section>
  </article>
</LayoutDefault>
<style>
  .system-photo {
    aspect-ratio: 1236 / 1086;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .system-photo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: left center;
  }
  .power-cable-photo {
    max-width: 440px;
    margin: 26px 0;
  }

  .room-measurement-images {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 220px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: start;
    margin: 28px 0;
  }
  .measurement-microphone img {
    max-width: 220px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .room-measurement-images {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .testing-dots {
    display: inline-block;
    animation: testing-dots 2s steps(1, end) infinite;
  }
  @keyframes testing-dots {
    0% {
      clip-path: inset(0 100% 0 0);
    }
    25% {
      clip-path: inset(0 66.6667% 0 0);
    }
    50% {
      clip-path: inset(0 33.3333% 0 0);
    }
    75% {
      clip-path: inset(0);
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .testing-dots {
      animation: none;
    }
  }

  video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .listening-videos {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .listening-videos {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .equipment-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 28px 0;
  }
  .equipment-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 18px;
  }
  .equipment-card img {
    height: 210px;
    object-fit: contain;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .speaker-equipment {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .speaker-equipment img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .equipment-note {
    color: var(--note-color);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .equipment-card h3 {
    font-size: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .equipment-card p {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .equipment-role {
    font: 12px/1.7 var(--note-font);
    color: var(--note-color);
  }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .speaker-equipment {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .speaker-equipment img {
      height: auto;
      max-height: 440px;
      object-fit: contain;
    }
    .equipment-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .hifi-page {
    max-width: 850px;
  }
  header {
    margin: 36px 0 28px;
  }
  h1,
  h2 {
    font-family: 'MyFont', monospace;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 54px);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 12px 0 22px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(27px, 4vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  p {
    line-height: 1.85;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  section {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  figure {
    margin: 0;
  }
  img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .cable-photos {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 440px);
    gap: 20px;
    margin: 26px 0;
  }
  figcaption {
    font: 12px/1.7 var(--note-font);
    color: var(--note-color);
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  dl {
    margin: 24px 0;
  }
  dl div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 140px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  dt {
    color: var(--note-color);
  }
  dd {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .speaker-photo {
    max-width: 440px;
    margin-top: 26px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .cable-photos {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    dl div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 5px;
    }
  }
</style>
